  "summary": "PR 1812 adds a test:sidecar-ci suite that brings 34 previously ungated sidecar test files under unconditional CI via an explicit frozen inventory, an exactly-once assignment guard, and strict inner-TAP validation through the existing runFixedSuite transport. No blocking findings for this exact reviewedHEAD.\n\nThe diff is internally consistent across all eight changed files. Inventory arithmetic is correct: 18 (sidecar) + 6 (security) + 34 (remaining) = 58 files total, which matches the hardcoded count assertion at sidecar-ci-inventory.test.mjs:25. Stage argument lengths are correct: SIDECAR_REMAINING_NODE_FILES (32 items) + '--test' = 33 for stage[0]; ['--import','tsx','--test'] + 2 tsx files = 5 for stage[1], matching the length assertions in mcp-suite-entry.test.mjs:66-68. The sidecar-remaining key is correctly added to SUITE_STAGES in mcp-suite-entry.mjs with the SUITE_STAGES key-set assertion updated to include it. The assertSidecarSmokeWiring function correctly verifies unconditional placement of all three smoke steps and is exercised by mutation proof row4 (removing the smoke step goes red) and by sidecar-ci-inventory.test.mjs:89-94. Five mutation proofs (key-health missing from list, unassigned-guard neutralised, duplicate-guard neutralised, smoke step removed, wrong suite identity in suite test) all exhibit genuine red transitions and are restored to green. The agentic gate and explicit QA passed all required suites at confirmed counts (test:sidecar-ci 13/0, test:sidecar 659/0, test:sec-hardening 69/0, test:workflow-security 59/0, test:pwa-deployment 26/0). Path-traversal guard in assertPath rejects '..' components and non-mjs/mts extensions. Build warnings (Vite configLoader native, chunk size, ineffective dynamic imports) are pre-existing and disclosed. Bundle remains within all policy limits (eager 2.84 MB / 2.85 MB cap, total 5.17 MB / 6 MB cap).\n\nOne nonblocking gap persists from the prior review: the two new test entry files (tests/sidecar-ci-inventory.test.mjs and tests/sidecar-ci-suite.test.mjs) are absent as explicit keys in targeted-tests-overrides.json. However, this gap is closed by the derived index: deriveScriptIndex parses the test:sidecar-ci command ('node --test tests/sidecar-ci-inventory.test.mjs tests/sidecar-ci-suite.test.mjs') and populates testFiles with both paths, so selectScripts will match and select test:sidecar-ci whenever either file is a changed path, without needing an override entry. The override keys would be redundant documentation; no actual coverage gap exists. The unconditional smoke step provides a further independent safety net."
